                <pb facs="0614" n="480" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg480"/>

                <head>No. 329.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Anderson to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-12-14"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 14,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Benson’s identity certain. Send officer to receive him at once. Denmark willing
                    to extradite without treaty. Key to Benson’s cipher dispatches found. Instruct
                    me to ask for copies of his telegrams sent and received here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Anderson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
